entity story                      # one story in a spec_file
  id                              # FUL-005
  file: one spec_file
  sentence
  role_name
  epic_id, optional
  text                            # the story as it stands in the file
  rules_text                      # its operations and examples only, normalised
  approvals: many approval
  version: count(approvals)
  state: approved if count(approvals) is more than 0
           and rules_text is approvals[-1]'s rules_text
         else draft
  may create: agent
  may read:   agent, operator
  may update: agent
  may delete: nobody

entity approval, part of story    # one block in the .edda.vc file
  version
  approved_at
  approved_by
  because, optional
  text                            # the whole story as approved
  rules_text

story a story is a draft until the operator approves it             # EDDA-004
  as a operator
  i want a story whose operations or examples differ from its newest
    approved copy to be a draft, whoever changed it
  so that nothing the agent writes counts until I have said yes
  epic: VC
  tags: version, approval

  operation state_of(story) returns story's state
    who: agent, operator

  example a new story is a draft
    given story fresh with id "FUL-010", approvals []
    when  agent asks state_of(fresh)
    then  done
          fresh's state is draft

  example a story that matches its newest approval is approved
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "R1"
          story same with id "FUL-005", rules_text "R1", approvals [a1]
    when  agent asks state_of(same)
    then  done
          same's state is approved

  example a changed rule makes a draft again
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "R1"
          story changed with id "FUL-005", rules_text "R2", approvals [a1]
    when  agent asks state_of(changed)
    then  done
          changed's state is draft

  example a changed label does not make a draft
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "R1", text "T1"
          story relabelled with id "FUL-005", rules_text "R1", text "T2",
            approvals [a1]
    when  agent asks state_of(relabelled)
    then  done
          relabelled's state is approved

story the operator approves a story and the copy is kept            # EDDA-005
  as a operator
  i want my yes to append the whole story as a new version to the
    .edda.vc file, with the date, my name and one line of because
  so that every approved version is kept exactly and the agent cannot
    write it
  epic: VC
  tags: version, approval

  operation approve(story, because)
    who: operator
    if story's state is approved,
      refuse: "nothing to approve: the story matches its newest version"
    if count(check(story's file)) is more than 0
      and any(p's kind is refused for p in check(story's file)),
      refuse: "the file does not check"
    when approve succeeds, ensure:
      count(story's approvals) is the old count(story's approvals) + 1
      story's approvals[-1]'s version is story's version
      story's approvals[-1]'s text is story's text
      story's approvals[-1]'s rules_text is story's rules_text
      story's approvals[-1]'s approved_by is the actor
      story's approvals[-1]'s approved_at is now
      story's approvals[-1]'s because is because
      story's state is approved

  example the first approval makes version 1
    given operator tuan
          story fresh with id "FUL-010", rules_text "R1", text "T1",
            approvals [], file good
          spec_file good with path "fixtures/order.edda", stories [fresh]
    when  tuan asks approve(fresh, "the shop asked for it") at 2026-10-01 14:00
    then  done
          fresh's version is 1
          fresh's approvals[-1]'s approved_by is tuan
          fresh's approvals[-1]'s because is "the shop asked for it"
          fresh's state is approved

  example approving an approved story is refused
    given operator tuan
          approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "R1"
          story same with id "FUL-005", rules_text "R1", approvals [a1],
            file good
          spec_file good with path "fixtures/order.edda", stories [same]
    when  tuan asks approve(same, "")
    then  refused: "nothing to approve: the story matches its newest version"
          same's version is 1

  example the agent may not approve
    given agent bot
          story fresh with id "FUL-010", rules_text "R1", approvals []
    when  bot asks approve(fresh, "")
    then  refused: "agent may not approve"

story the operator sees what changed before saying yes               # EDDA-006
  as a operator
  i want the difference between the story in the file and its newest
    approved copy as added, changed and removed sentences
  so that I read the change, not the whole story, every time
  epic: VC
  tags: version, diff

  operation diff(story) returns
    [change for change in sentence_changes(story's approvals[-1]'s text, story's text)]
    who: agent, operator
    note: sentence_changes is a level 2 helper; a sentence is one line
      of the story with its indentation removed

  example an added refusal shows as added
    given approval a1 with version 1,
            text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
          story grown with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\"\n  if the order's units_sent is more than 0,\n    refuse: \"already sent\""
    when  operator asks diff(grown)
    then  done
          count(diff(grown)) is 2
          diff(grown)[0]'s kind is added
          diff(grown)[0]'s sentence is "if the order's units_sent is more than 0,"
